Trouble?

255
00:14:28,490 --> 00:14:30,610
Your sister stood me up the other night.

256
00:14:30,820 --> 00:14:34,450
Oh, no. Don't you hate it when people aren't there for you?

257
00:14:36,410 --> 00:14:39,370
- Did you try calling her?     - I've been trying for two days.

258
00:14:39,620 --> 00:14:42,380
When I called the restaurant, they said she was too busy to talk.

259
00:14:42,630 --> 00:14:45,300
I can't believe she's blowing me off.

260
00:14:53,430 --> 00:14:56,760

261
00:15:04,730 --> 00:15:05,770
Hey.

262
00:15:06,940 --> 00:15:08,320
Oh.

263
00:15:09,740 --> 00:15:11,400
Um, you got a minute?

264
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:14,490
Um, yeah, I'm just working.

265
00:15:22,790 --> 00:15:24,630
- So...     - Uh-huh?

266
00:15:26,340 --> 00:15:28,550
Um, oh, I got you a birthday present.

267
00:15:28,880 --> 00:15:30,340
Oh, wow, you remembered.

268
00:15:35,050 --> 00:15:38,310
Oh. It's a Judy Jetson Thermos.

269
00:15:38,520 --> 00:15:39,810
Right. Like the kind you...

270
00:15:40,020 --> 00:15:41,180
Right.

271
00:15:41,850 --> 00:15:44,020
Oh, I got something for you too.

272
00:15:44,230 --> 00:15:45,440
How'd you know I was coming?

273
00:15:45,610 --> 00:15:48,780
Um, yeah, um, "twin" thing.

274
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:53,360
I can't believe you did this.

275
00:15:53,570 --> 00:15:55,370
I can't believe you...

276
00:15:55,620 --> 00:15:57,240
...did this.

277
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:03,670
So, what's the deal with, um, you and Joey?

278
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:05,830
Oh, right.

279
00:16:06,040 --> 00:16:08,840
He is so great. But that's over.

280
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:11,590
- Does he know?     - Who?

281
00:16:12,470 --> 00:16:17,100
Joey. You know, um, ahem, he's really nutsy about you.

282
00:16:17,550 --> 00:16:19,060
He is? Why?

283
00:16:19,350 --> 00:16:21,220
- You got me.     - Right.

284
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:22,520
Excuse me...

285
00:16:22,770 --> 00:16:25,400
...doesn't this come with a side salad?

286
00:16:27,020 --> 00:16:28,860
So, um, are you gonna call him?

287
00:16:29,070 --> 00:16:31,940
- What, you think he likes me?     - No. Joey.

288
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:37,070
Oh. No, no. He is so smart. He'll figure it out.

289
00:16:37,320 --> 00:16:38,950
Do you want some chicken?

290
00:16:39,740 --> 00:16:42,580
No, no. No food with a face, remember?

291
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,120
You have not changed.

292
00:16:45,460 --> 00:16:46,870
Yeah, you too.

293
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:53,090
- Hi. Remember us?     - Mm-hm.

294
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:57,550
Um, yeah, you just called about needing a signature on the admissions form?

295
00:16:57,800 --> 00:17:00,260
Well, it turns out we need a whole new one.

296
00:17:00,510 --> 00:17:02,560
Because, um, you see...

297
00:17:03,100 --> 00:17:05,230
...I put the wrong name again.

298
00:17:05,940 --> 00:17:08,770
- Because, um...     - You're that stupid.

299
00:17:10,020 --> 00:17:12,730
I am. I'm that stupid.

300
00:17:13,320 --> 00:17:15,820
Yeah, and I'm just gonna pay for this with a check.

301
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:18,070
You know, your insurance will cover that.

302
00:17:18,280 --> 00:17:20,870
Yeah, I know. I'm just not that bright either.

303
00:17:23,120 --> 00:17:24,580
Okay, worst case scenario:

304
00:17:24,910 --> 00:17:28,210
Say you never feel like a father.

305
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:32,340
Say your son never feels connected to you as one.

306
00:17:32,840 --> 00:17:36,470
Say all of his relationships are affected by this.

307
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:38,380
Do you have a point?

308
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:41,510
You know, you'd think I would.

309
00:17:44,640 --> 00:17:46,520
What's up with the simian?

310
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:49,650
It's just a fur ball.

311
00:17:51,610 --> 00:17:53,150
Okay, whose turn is it?

312
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:55,320
Yours. I just got 43 points for "kidney."

313
00:17:55,740 --> 00:17:59,070
No, you got zero points for "idney."

314
00:17:59,280 --> 00:18:01,620
I had a K. Where's my K?

315
00:18:08,710 --> 00:18:11,250
You've got to help me. My monkey swallowed a K.

316
00:18:11,250 --> 00:18:13,200
Get that animal out of here.

317
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:15,660
You don't understand. The animal hospital is way across town.

318
00:18:15,660 --> 00:18:17,010
He's choking. I don't know what to do.

319
00:18:17,220 --> 00:18:19,880
- What's going on?     - Marcel swallowed a Scrabble tile.

320
00:18:22,010 --> 00:18:25,640
Excuse me. This hospital is for people.

321
00:18:25,850 --> 00:18:28,230
Lady, he is people. He has a name, okay?

322
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:30,060
He watches Jeopardy...

323
00:18:30,270 --> 00:18:33,020
...he touches himself when nobody's watching.

324
00:18:34,110 --> 00:18:35,610
Please, have a heart.

325
00:18:35,820 --> 00:18:38,070
- I'll take a look at him.     - Oh, thank you.

326
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:39,360
- Michael.     - Rachel.

327
00:18:39,570 --> 00:18:40,610
- What?     - Monica.

328
00:18:40,780 --> 00:18:42,620
- Oh.     - Hi.

329
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,170
Hey.

330
00:18:57,090 --> 00:18:58,260
Urs.

331
00:18:58,630 --> 00:19:00,760
What are you doing here? I've been trying to call you.

332
00:19:01,930 --> 00:19:02,970
Listen, um...

333
00:19:03,140 --> 00:19:07,010
Don't say "listen." I know that "listen." I've said that "listen."

334
00:19:08,270 --> 00:19:09,310
I'm sorry.

335
00:19:10,350 --> 00:19:12,350
I don't get it. What happened?

336
00:19:12,600 --> 00:19:15,020
What about everything you said under the bridge?

337
00:19:15,980 --> 00:19:18,320
Yeah, um, ahem...

338
00:19:19,110 --> 00:19:21,740
You know, just forget about what I said under the bridge.

339
00:19:21,950 --> 00:19:25,160
I was talking crazy that night. I was so drunk.

340
00:19:26,830 --> 00:19:27,870
You don't drink.

341
00:19:28,660 --> 00:19:30,580
That's right, I don't.

342
00:19:31,170 --> 00:19:33,080
But I was drunk on you.

343
00:19:34,250 --> 00:19:37,040
- Oh, Urs.     - But, yeah, so it's not gonna work.

344
00:19:37,750 --> 00:19:40,420
Why? Is it because I'm friends with Phoebe?

345
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:44,470
If it was, would you stop hanging out with her?

346
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:47,680
No.

347
00:19:47,890 --> 00:19:50,240
No, I couldn't do that.

348
00:19:50,390 --> 00:19:53,100
Um, then, yeah, it's because of Phoebe.

349
00:19:54,520 --> 00:19:57,270
So you know, it's either her or me.

350
00:19:58,730 --> 00:20:01,860
Then, uh... Then I'm sorry.

351
00:20:06,490 --> 00:20:08,080
You know...

352
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:10,620
...you're gonna be really, really hard to get over.

353
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:12,500
I know.

354
00:20:18,710 --> 00:20:23,130
I don't know whether it's just because we're breaking up or what...

355
00:20:23,380 --> 00:20:25,380
...but you have never looked so beautiful.

356
00:20:26,050 --> 00:20:27,090
Really?

357
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:59,420
- Pheebs?     - Yeah.

358
00:21:10,100 --> 00:21:11,390
He looks so tiny.

359
00:21:13,060 --> 00:21:14,810
- We just got the message.     - Is he all right?

360
00:21:15,020 --> 00:21:17,350
Yeah, the doctor got the K out.

361
00:21:17,980 --> 00:21:20,310
He also found an M and an O.

362
00:21:22,230 --> 00:21:25,070
We think he was trying to spell out "monkey."

363
00:21:31,410 --> 00:21:34,870
The doctor says he'll be fine. He's just sleeping now.

364
00:21:36,540 --> 00:21:38,330
So you feel like a dad yet?

365
00:21:38,580 --> 00:21:40,330
No. Why?

366
00:21:40,710 --> 00:21:44,340
Hey, come on, you came through. You did what you had to do.

367
00:21:44,550 --> 00:21:46,050
That is very dad.

368
00:21:46,220 --> 00:21:47,760
Oh, look, he's waking up.

369
00:21:48,090 --> 00:21:50,550
Hey, fella. How you doing?

